1. Difference between var, let, and const
Feature	var	let	const
| Feature    | var      | let   | const |
| ---------- | -------- | ----- | ----- |
| Scope      | Function | Block | Block |
| Re-declare | Yes      | No    | No    |
| Re-assign  | Yes      | Yes   | No    |

Example:
var a = 10;
let b = 20;
const c = 30;
const object properties can still change.

What is hoisting?
JavaScript moves declarations to the top during compilation.
console.log(a);
var a = 5;
Output:
undefined
Because only declaration is hoisted, not initialization.
3. Difference between == and ===
5 == "5"   // true
5 === "5"  // false
== checks value only
=== checks value + datatype
Always prefer ===.

